   "text": "Skip to feedback\nSkip to main content\nAn official website of the United States government\nSearch or ask anything\nAsk DOI Anything - How Can We Help?\nWhat national wildlife refuges are near me?\nDo I need a permit to fish on a national wildlife refuge?\nWhat is the Junior Duck Stamp contest?\nHow can kids get involved with wildlife refuges?\nUtility (Top) navigation\nPasses\nPermits\nDuck Stamps\nReport a Crime\nExperience America\nPlaces to Go\nSpecies\nLearn\nServices\nOur Work\nIowa Wetland Management District\nIowa Wetland Management District\nThe Iowa Wetland Management District includes 75 waterfowl production areas encompassing more than 25,000 acres scattered throughout 18 counties in north-central Iowa. The goal of the district is to restore and protect enough wetland and grassland habitat to meet the needs of prairie wildlife,...\nNational Wildlife Refuge\nTitonka,\nIA\nRefine Map\nAmenities\nBoundaries\nLocations\nAmenities\nParking Lot\nBoundaries\nBailey Creek WPA\nBarringer Slough WPA\nBays Branch WPA\nBeaver Dam WPA\nBig Wall Lake WPA\nBison WPA\nBlackhawk Marsh WPA\nBlazing Star WPA\nBlue-wing WPA\nBluestem WPA\nBluewing Marsh WPA\nBobolink WPA\nBurr Oak WPA\nCayler Prairie WPA\nCheever Lake WPA\nCopp Prairie WPA\nCory Marsh WPA\nCrystal Lake WPA\nDan Greene WPA\nDewey's Pasture WPA\nDewey's Pasture WPA\nDiamond Lake WPA\nDickcissel WPA\nDucks Unlimited Marsh WPA\nDugout Creek WPA\nDunbar Slough WPA\nEagle Flats WPA\nEagle Lake WPA\nEagle Lake WPA\nElk Creek WPA\nElk Lake WPA\nErrington Marsh WPA\nFallow Marsh WPA\nFour Mile WPA\nGarlock Slough WPA\nGood Neighbors Marsh WPA\nGoose Lake WPA\nGrass Lake WPA\nHarlontown Slough WPA\nHarrier WPA\nHogsback Marsh WPA\nIngham Lake WPA\nIowa Lake Marsh WPA\nIowa National Heritage Foundation\nIowa National Heritage Foundation WPA\nIowa Natural Heritage Foundation WPA\nJemmerson Slough WPA\nKettleson Hogsback WPA\nKiowa Marsh WPA\nLake Edwards WPA\nLakin Slough WPA\nLower Morse Lake WPA\nMallard WPA\nMaynard Reece WPA\nMcClurg WPA\nMeredith Marsh WPA\nMyre Slough WPA\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nN/A\nOlaf WPA\nPalo Alto WPA\nPickerel Lake WPA\nPilot Knob WPA\nPintail WPA\nPlover WPA\nPrairie Smoke WPA\nRice Lake WPA\nSandpiper WPA\nSantee Prairie WPA\nShimon Marsh WPA\nSmith WPA\nSnake Creek WPA\nSpring Run WPA\nState Line Marsh WPA\nSwan Lake WPA\nTeal Basins WPA\nTomahawk Marsh WPA\nTuttle Lake WPA\nTwelve Mile WPA\nUnion Hills WPA\nWapati WPA\nWellnitz WPA\nWelsh Lake WPA\nWest Lake Okoboji WPA\nWest Swan Lake WPA\nWinnebago County WPA\nWood Duck Marsh WPA\nYager Slough WPA\nLocations\nIowa Wetland Management District\n+\n−\nLeaflet | © OpenStreetMap\nFooter Menu - Legal\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nWork with Us\nPolicies\nOffice of Civil Rights\nSearch\nFWS.GOV\nAn official website of the Department of the Interior\nHelp improve this site\nDisclaimer\nThe boundary map layer was compiled by the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service. Although these boundaries represent lands administered by the U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service, not all areas are open to the public. Some fragile habitats need to be protected from human traffic, and some management areas are closed. The public is urged to contact specific national wildlife refuges or other conservation areas before visiting.\nDo not show this message again\nContinue",
